10. Design-Build-Test-Learn Integration

APT is compatible with the AI-driven design-build-test-learn paradigm.

The biological engineering loop becomes:

D \rightarrow B \rightarrow T \rightarrow L \rightarrow D,

where D is design, B is biological implementation, T is testing, and L is learning.

APT extends this by adding an explicit control-theoretic layer:

\text{Design} \rightarrow \text{Predict} \rightarrow \text{Verify} \rightarrow \text{Test} \rightarrow \text{Observe} \rightarrow \text{Update}.

The predictive verification step is what distinguishes APT from open-loop design-build-test-learn cycles.

---

11. The Adaptive Therapeutic Loop

The complete architecture is a closed loop. The patient or biological system is observed through sensing, which feeds state estimation, which updates the patient digital twin, which informs the virtual cell and tissue model, which drives AI therapeutic design, which is constrained by a predictive safety filter, which authorizes a programmable intervention, which acts on the biological system, whose response is measured, and the cycle repeats.

APT is explicitly a computational-molecular closed loop. The sensor is multi-omic profiling and imaging; the processor is AI state estimation and model-predictive control; the actuator is programmable RNA plus LNP delivery. The loop operates on hours-to-days timescales between doses, unlike implantable closed-loop devices that operate on milliseconds to minutes.

